From 65b97e3e3fc32c3fed92a5b7cab18c9aba344880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@localhost>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 22:12:17 -0400
Subject: xe: advertise HW_VIDEO_ENCODER on linear RGB32 combos (direct-RGB
 VDENC source)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Without these combos an ABGR8888 allocation carrying encoder usage
fails drv_get_combination, and cros_gralloc's fallback silently strips
BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER on retry (cros_gralloc_driver.cc) — so the
64-row height alignment for VDENC source reads never applied and the
c2-va direct-RGB path fell back to VPP on every frame. Advertise
encoder usage for the four linear 32bpp RGB formats (linear only, like
the NV12 combo). Verified end-to-end on the xe VF: gralloc0 usage
0x10303 -> use_flags 0x4224 -> 2048-row BO, direct encode at 3760x1992
with zero VCS CAT faults and a clean decoded stream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I2b8e64d17c5a90f3ab46ed82c1d97e0a5b3c4d21
---
 xe.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xe.c b/xe.c
index a46a843..cbdfca8 100644
--- a/xe.c
+++ b/xe.c
@@ -166,6 +166,24 @@ static int xe_add_combinations(struct driver *drv)
 	/* P010 linear can be used for scanout too. */
 	drv_modify_combination(drv, DRM_FORMAT_P010, &metadata_linear, BO_USE_SCANOUT);
 
+	/*
+	 * Linear 32bpp RGB as a VDENC encode source (the c2-va direct-RGB
+	 * path: the encoder imports the composited RGB buffer straight into
+	 * libva, EncSliceLP does the CSC). Without these combos the encoder
+	 * usage request fails drv_get_combination and cros_gralloc silently
+	 * strips BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER on retry — the buffer then misses the
+	 * CTB-64 height alignment the engine's reads require. Linear only: the
+	 * tiled combos must not advertise encoder usage.
+	 */
+	drv_modify_combination(drv, DRM_FORMAT_ABGR8888, &metadata_linear,
+			       BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER);
+	drv_modify_combination(drv, DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888, &metadata_linear,
+			       BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER);
+	drv_modify_combination(drv, DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888, &metadata_linear,
+			       BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER);
+	drv_modify_combination(drv, DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888, &metadata_linear,
+			       BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER);
+
 	/*
 	 * Android also frequently requests YV12 formats for some camera implementations
 	 * (including the external provider implementation).
